          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ডাল (ḍāl) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from dāla, \"split peas\" (CDIAL 6309). CDIAL asks whether it is one word with another dāla, \"piece split off\"."
            }
          ]
